(Kaikeel Handbook Lite: Release Checklist) Tj T*
(\(Fictional sample document for the DocQA demo.\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(VERSIONING) Tj T*
(Every release gets a semantic version number: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH.) Tj T*
(Increase PATCH for bug fixes, MINOR for backwards-compatible features,) Tj T*
(and MAJOR for breaking changes. The first client release is 0.1.0.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(CHANGELOG) Tj T*
(Move the entries under Unreleased into a new section named after the version,) Tj T*
(with the release date. Group entries as Added, Changed, Fixed and Removed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(TAGGING) Tj T*
(Create an annotated git tag such as v0.1.0 on the merge commit in main.) Tj T*
(The handover zip archive is always built from the tag, never from a branch.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
